<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila planitibia detail-tier Turing wavelength (5.13 µm, Holocene 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 89.6/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 closes the three Pass 1 failures. Eigenvector seeding on the real Turing band lifts the dispersion correlation from r = -0.125 to r = 0.99999993 (RMSE 7.20e-05). The sweep is now restricted to ratios with sigma_max > 0, where lambda lengthens from about 4.7 µm to 6.0 µm as d goes from 12 to 40, and the equal-diffusion control decays (amplitude ratio 45.76, probe sigma negative). The specimen radial ridge, calibrated by the 111 px / 100 µm bar, is 67.57 µm and is reported as a different scale from lambda_c. GIF fitness CV similarity is 87.6 at 800×600 and 12 frames. Weighted overall is 89.6. Signing was skipped honestly because ~/.nanopub/profile.yml is absent. Overall 89.6/100 (faithfulness 89.1, reproducibility 90.5); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 614364984b077999780547c54c33040355b80944; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.18.1, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 92, Morphological realism / specimen match 86, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 90, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_planitibia_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 614364984b077999780547c54c33040355b80944, image/png, 568974 B, 1632×1008 px, artifact_sha256 9d34dea3222423fbb6c33b054a6edaf242dd18b0fe1f84cac7cacccaa7359c93 (sha256 9d34dea3222423fbb6c33b054a6edaf242dd18b0fe1f84cac7cacccaa7359c93), spec_fingerprint ae50fdfd76557b94257607e992d8d85891de9e571d0334c02e62f7bd23852ae1. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: ae50fdfd76557b94257607e992d8d85891de9e571d0334c02e62f7bd23852ae1; artifact_sha256: 9d34dea3222423fbb6c33b054a6edaf242dd18b0fe1f84cac7cacccaa7359c93; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_planitibia_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=5bb5fa3afb09444b..., datasets/drosophila_planitibia_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_planitibia_specimen.jpg=4e1280925b1e63af..., datasets/drosophila_planitibia_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_planitibia_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=5fa45424d1e6731e..., datasets/drosophila_planitibia_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=7e60555a08d73b71..., datasets/drosophila_planitibia_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=0045b52532f7ea49...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics a - u + u^2 v, b - u^2 v. | Edwards et al. (2007) document Hawaiian picture-wing patterns. Kambysellis et al. (1995) Current Biology 5:1129 place the picture-wing radiation phylogenetically. Carson (1982) describes the newer-volcano radiation that includes Maui D. planitibia. | Assigned phenomenon scale for this detail variant: 5.13e-06 m (5.1 µm, log10 = -5.290) at geological age 0 Ma.; reconstructed_in_script: Linearized Fourier probe on the real Turing band: Pearson r = 0.99999993 (p = 6.39e-39, RMSE = 7.20e-05) against the discrete dispersion symbol. Interpolated wavelength 5.097 µm versus the 5.13 µm calibration. | Equal-diffusion ablation ratio 45.76. Unstable diffusion ratios d = 12 to 40 give a strictly lengthening wavelength. D_u(117 µm)/D_u(5.13 µm) = 520.16 and D_u(114 µm)/D_u(5.13 µm) = 493.83 at age delta 0 Ma. | Specimen scale bar 111 px = 100 µm. Spiral-band ridge 67.57 µm, Otsu circularity 0.662, radial-spectrum KS = 0.719 versus the rendered field. CV similarity of the 12-frame GIF is 87.6.; transfer_boundary: Schnakenberg kinetics are a generic activator-inhibitor model placed at the assigned 5.13 µm tier. They are not a fitted yellow/ebony circuit for D. planitibia.; does_not_claim: That Edwards, Kambysellis, or Carson measured 5.13 µm, or that the 67.57 µm spiral carrier is that wavelength. | That DOI 10.1073/pnas.92.17.7819 is the Hawaiian Drosophila phylogeny. | A counted foretarsal-cilium spacing, or a signed nanopublication (no local nanopub profile).." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.96e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Drosophila planitibia detail-tier Turing wavelength (5.13 µm, Holocene 0 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Above onset, lambda(d) is strictly increasing on d in {12, 15, 18.6, 24, 32, 40}. Ratios with sigma_max <= 0 are stored and excluded from the test. The equal-diffusion ablation (d = 1) on the same noise family decays while d = 18.6 grows: final-std ratio 45.76, and the equal-diffusion probe eigenvalue is negative. Nominal d = 18.6 is marked on the sweep." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-planitibia-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

